//! The AT24C128C I2C-compatible serial EEPROM, Microchip (Atmel), 128 Kbit (16,384 x 8), in the
//! 8-lead SOIC 150 mil package (package drawing code SN), order code AT24C128C-SSHM-T: the
//! U17 of ORBIT. ORBIT's schematic gives the part no value and no LCSC number; its footprint
//! `SOIC127P600X175-8N` is the 8-lead SOIC of 1.27 mm pitch, 6.0 mm over the leads. The
//! order code is the one LCSC and JLCPCB list for it in that package (C6478); it is not ORBIT's.
//!
//! The pin table was WRITTEN BY HAND from Microchip's datasheet "AT24C128C: I2C-Compatible
//! (Two-Wire) Serial EEPROM 128-Kbit (16,384 x 8)" (DS20006110A, November 2018, 41 pages; the
//! file read, fetched on 2026-11-10, is a mirror of Microchip's PDF:
//! <https://static.chipdip.ru/lib/144/DOC006144019.pdf>): section 1 "Package Types" (printed
//! page 4) and Table 2-1 "Pin Function Table" with sections 2.1 to 2.6 (printed pages 5 and 6)
//! for the pads, names and what each pin is. The datasheet is copyrighted: the numbers and
//! names are facts, the words and the arrangement here are ours.
//!
//! The kinds: `A0`, `A1`, `A2` and `WP` are `input` (the datasheet says they may be left
//! floating, as they are pulled down inside, and recommends a known level: they are not marked
//! `optional`, so a board connects each), `SCL` is `input`, `SDA` is `bidirectional` (the datasheet
//! calls it an open-drain bidirectional pin, section 2.3, page 5), `GND` and `VCC` are `power`.
//!
//! The two-wire interface is an `I2c` (`std::bus`) in which the EEPROM is a target, as its
//! section 2.3 says of `SDA` and its section 6 of the addressing (a controller starts every
//! transfer), so a board joins the bus with `~`.
//!
//! What is deliberately left out: the levels, ratings, bus timing and the supply range
//! (1.7 V to 5.5 V), so the part is a boundary of the design and the checks that need a number
//! are listed as not evaluated; and the other packages of the table.

import std::bus::{I2c, I2cRole}

/// The AT24C128C, a 128 Kbit serial EEPROM with a two-wire interface, in the 8-lead SOIC. Pin
/// names are the datasheet's; the pad numbers are those of its 8-lead SOIC column.
part At24C128C {
    .designator &= "U"

    /// The two-wire interface: `SDA` and `SCL`.
    .i2c: I2c
    .i2c.role &= I2cRole::Target

    pins "SOIC-8" {
        //  pin   kind           name   pads
        .a0    input          "A0"   "1"
        .a1    input          "A1"   "2"
        .a2    input          "A2"   "3"
        .gnd   power          "GND"  "4"
        .i2c.sda bidirectional "SDA" "5"
        .i2c.scl input         "SCL" "6"
        .wp    input          "WP"   "7"
        .vcc   power          "VCC"  "8"
    }

    .package: Package
    catalog at24c128c by .mpn { .mpn, .package }
}
